    "Based on your selected strategy, we estimate your exercise-related energy burn using:\n\n• Eat Less → BMR × 0.20  \n• Balanced → BMR × 0.55  \n• Move More → BMR × 0.725  \n\nThese values are based on the same PAL system used in the TDEE calculation." : {

    },
    "Before we start, these details will help us create useful predictions." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在开始之前，这些信息将帮助我们生成有用的预测结果。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "BMI: %@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "BMI：%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "BMR is the number of calories your body needs at rest — just to keep you alive (breathing, circulating blood, etc.).\n\nWe use the Mifflin–St Jeor Equation:\n\n• For men:\n  BMR = 10 × weight (kg) + 6.25 × height (cm) – 5 × age + 5\n\n• For women:\n  BMR = 10 × weight (kg) + 6.25 × height (cm) – 5 × age – 161\n\n• If you prefer not to specify gender:\n  We skip the +5 or –161 adjustment.\n\n• If you don’t enter your age:\n  We assume a default of 30 years old." : {

    },
    "But don't pack your bags, it's 900°F there and rains sulfuric acid!" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
